        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-03-24T14:58:27+00:00",
        "description": "<p>Gemini Embedding 2 can project raw video directly into a 768-dimensional vector space alongside text. No transcription, no frame captioning, no intermediate text. A query like \"green car cutting me off\" is directly comparable to a 30-second video clip at the vector level.<p>I used this to build a CLI that indexes hours of footage into ChromaDB, then searches it with natural language and auto-trims the matching clip. Demo video on the GitHub README.\nIndexing costs ~$2.50/hr of footage. Still-frame detection skips idle chunks, so security camera / sentry mode footage is much cheaper.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47503617\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47503617</a></p>\n<p>Points: 26</p>\n<p># Comments: 8</p>",
